    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d519">

                <pb facs="0593" n="581" sameAs="frus:frus1941v02/pg581"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">740.00118 European War 1939/754: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Consul at Leopoldville</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Mallon</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of State </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Leopoldville</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1941-11-02T23:00:00+01:00">November 2,
                            1941—11 p.m.</date>
                        <lb/> [Received November 3—10:42 a.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>For Miles from Cunningham.</p>
                <p>“Reference your October 23, 11 p.m. Have given only one press interview to
                    Sedgewick <hi rendition="#italic">New York Times</hi> whom I know and trust.
                    Statements made to him were based on facts which I have found and verified. I
                    saw his copy before he sent it and it had my approval based upon my knowledge
                    and judgment. I am not responsible for whatever news editor may have done with
                    his text. As to my duty I have spent 16 hours per day finding and classifying
                    facts in a country where most people cannot work more than 6 or 8 per day and my
                    conscience is clear. We are received everywhere as ‘American Mission’ and
                    arithmetic having made me senior member I am recognized as Chief of Mission.
                    Before I left United States, Atherton, State Department, said to me ‘Remember,
                    you are Chief of the Mission’. Have just completed over 8,000 kilometers of fact
                    finding and results will follow day by day. Leave again Wednesday<anchor n="54"
                        xml:id="d519-f1"/> for more fact finding. [Cunningham.]”</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Mallon</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
